// wave_defense stress fixture (task #243): spawner self-cast that
// summons N monsters per wave.
//
// `summon "monster" <count>` lowers via the `summon` arm of
// `dsl_compiler::ability_lower::lower_effect_stmt` to
// `EffectOp::Summon { template_hash, count, lifetime_ticks }`.
// template_hash is the FxHash of the "monster" ident; count is a
// literal u8 baked into the program at lowering time (= constant
// per-wave size for THIS slice — see wave_defense.sim's "WAVE-SIZE
// PLUMBING — TASK #243 DECISION" comment for the deferral rationale).
//
// The dispatcher writes one EffectSummonApplied chronicle record
// (kind=62) per cast, packing (template_hash, count, lifetime_ticks)
// into the chronicle's payload slots. The runtime drains those records
// after each step() and calls `apply_summon_event_to_state` (engine
// primitive) to allocate `count` new monster agent slots at the
// spawner's `agent_pos`. Per
// `crates/engine/src/ability/apply.rs::apply_summon_event_to_state`
// the new slots come from the deterministic agent pool freelist; with
// no per-template stat resolution today (the SummonTemplateRegistry is
// a follow-up — see the comment in apply.rs:1556), every spawned slot
// gets `AgentSpawn::default()` which the runtime overrides with
// per-fixture monster stats (hp, alive, creature_type) immediately
// after the call.
//
// `cooldown: 3s` (= 30 ticks) matches the .sim's `wave_period` config
// value so the cooldown gate stays in the verb's `when` clause and the
// registry's program.cooldown_ticks field is informational only.

ability SpawnWave {
    target: self
    cooldown: 3s
    hint: utility

    summon "monster" 8 [UTILITY: 100]
}
